%I A399809 #6 Sep 14 2026 19:15:15
%S A399809 1,1,1,1,11,494,1429895,878019990244
%N A399809 Number of Hausdorff antichains of nonempty proper subsets of an n-set.
%C A399809 An antichain F of subsets of X is Hausdorff if for every two distinct elements x,y in X there exist A,B in F such that x is in A, y is in B, and A intersect B is empty.
%H A399809 Goran Kilibarda, <a href="https://doi.org/10.2298/PIM140406001K">Enumeration of certain classes of antichains</a>, Publications de l'Institut Mathématique, 97 (111) (2015), 69-87.
%F A399809 For a simple graph Q on [n], let D_Q be the graph whose vertices are the nonempty proper subsets of [n], with distinct A and B adjacent iff A is contained in B or B is contained in A, or A and B are disjoint and there exist x in A and y in B such that {x,y} is an edge of Q. Then a(n) = Sum_Q (-1)^|E(Q)| i(D_Q), where the sum is over all simple graphs Q on [n] and i(G) is the number of independent sets of G.
%e A399809 For n=4, writing 1,2,3,4 for the singletons and 12,13,14,23,24,34 for the 2-subsets, the 11 Hausdorff antichains are {1,2,3,4}; {12,13,24,34}, {12,14,23,34}, {13,14,23,24}; {12,13,14,23,24}, {12,13,14,23,34}, {12,13,14,24,34}, {12,13,23,24,34}, {12,14,23,24,34}, {13,14,23,24,34}; and {12,13,14,23,24,34}. Hence a(4)=11.
%Y A399809 Cf. A398881, A000372.
%K A399809 nonn,more,new
